 "timing_rationale": "Coincident: an annualised month of revenue moves with current usage and is reported within weeks, when it is reported at all.",
 "tracker_interpretation": "Several application companies report run-rates in the hundreds of millions within two or three years of launch, but every figure is a company statement, a press leak or an analyst's estimate, and definitions differ (run-rate, ARR, contracted ARR, bookings).",
 "unit": "USD",
 "unpublished_reason": "No direction rule fits yet: each company reports on its own irregular dates and definitions, so there is no single series to read for a trend. The rows are on /series and in Ask; the indicator publishes once a rule over companies with like definitions is written and reviewed.",
 "updated_at": "2026-09-25",
 "valve_measured": null,
 "why_it_matters": "Whether the application layer keeps a share of the surplus depends on its revenue growing as model prices fall. Until now the tracker had no revenue for any application company."
